# Files Docker leaves out of the image. One pattern per line; lines starting with # are notes.
# A pattern starting with **/ matches in this folder or any folder below it.

# Git's history and settings: the program doesn't need them, and they can hold old secrets.
.git

# Python and Node.js add-on folders, in any folder: big, and rebuilt inside the image if needed.
**/.venv
**/venv
node_modules

# Python's saved bytecode, in any folder.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Secret files such as API keys, in any folder: they must never go into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Key files and logs, in any folder: keys are secrets, and logs can hold private details.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.log

# Spreadsheet exports, in any folder: they can hold real listings, and this version reads none.
**/*.csv

# Claude Code and Superpowers settings, used while building, not while running.
.claude
.superpowers

# The task plans and the code review: people read them, the program doesn't need them.
docs
REVIEW.md
